who traversed on or near the Monon Hybrid trail on the day of the murders. The sketch had taken months to construct due to the gradual pace at which these witnesses came forward, coupled with the time it took for investigators to verify and collate details between their statements. The male suspect was described as Caucasian, between 5'6 and 5'10 inches tall, weighing 180 to 220 pounds, with reddish brown hair and an unknown eye color. The sketch depicted him as middle-aged with a square face, short hair, small, wide-set eyes and a large nose, with a neatly trimmed goatee. In the drawing, he wore a flat cap, but investigators established this detail might not be accurate, as multiple witnesses were unable to agree on it. They advised the

